WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:00.874
(bright music)

00:00:00.874 --> 00:00:03.030
- [Reporter] A federal jury
found Donald Trump liable

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.340
for the sexual abuse and defamation

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.530
of writer E. Jean Carroll and ordered him

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.500
to pay $5 million in damages.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.333
- [Speaker] How do you feel?

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:12.390
- [Carroll] Very happy.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.280
- [Reporter] Trump called
the verdict a disgrace

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.820
in a message on his social
media network, Truth Social.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.250
Corinne Ramey covers
New York investigations

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.080
into Donald Trump, and has been following

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.700
the civil trial for the journal.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.200
She explains what you need to know

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.960
about the case and what the
consequences are for Trump.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.750
(bright music continues)

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.200
- This lawsuit was filed
in 2022 by E. Jean Carroll,

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.600
a writer and advice columnist.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.060
She alleged in the lawsuit
that Donald Trump raped her

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.460
in the dressing room
of Bergdorf Goodman's,

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.190
a Manhattan department
store in the mid 1990s.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:48.150
- He put his shoulder against
me to hold me against the wall

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.590
and at that point, I realized

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.750
that I was in a very difficult situation.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.890
- Her lawyers tried to show

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.440
that Trump had, what they call, an MO,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.680
that he sexually assaulted
women in similar ways,

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.770
and they did this through both
the accounts of two women,

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:05.970
but also by playing the
2005 Access Hollywood tape.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.320
- [Trump] You Know, I'm
automatically attracted

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.880
to beautiful, I just start kissing them.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:09.937
It's like a magnet.
(person laughs)

00:01:09.937 --> 00:01:11.337
You just kiss.
(person continues to laugh)

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.170
I don't even wait.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.197
And when you're a star,
they let you do it.

00:01:14.197 --> 00:01:15.614
You can do anything.
- [Speaker] Whatever you want.

00:01:15.614 --> 00:01:17.329
- Grab 'em by the.

00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:18.440
(person continues to laugh)

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.530
You can do anything.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:22.320
- Trump's side chose not to
present any witnesses at trial,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.880
but they said one reason for this

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.430
is because his defense was,

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:27.750
essentially that it never happened,

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.480
that her story was a
lie, it was inconsistent.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.950
Trump has said he doesn't know Carroll

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.270
and that he's never met her.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.367
- [Prosecutor] Now, when you say in here,

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:41.367
"I don't know this woman,
and have no idea who she is,"

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.600
even though you're
using the present tense,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.490
you're referring back to your knowledge

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.590
as of when she first made the allegation.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.300
- I still don't know this woman.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.740
I think she's a whack job.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.670
I have no idea.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.200
I don't know anything about this woman

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.253
other than what I read in
stories and what I hear.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.600
I know nothing about her

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.250
- In the lawsuit, she also alleges

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:09.780
that Trump defamed her in
a 2022 social media post

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.830
in which he called her
account a hoax and a lie

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.680
and said, "She wasn't my type."

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.450
Carroll asked for damages for
both defamation and battery.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.180
One of her lawyers said
in a closing argument

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.360
that for aging Carroll, the
case was not about the money.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.740
For Trump, the immediate impact

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.660
is he'll have to pay the damages

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.640
that were ordered by the jury.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.140
- This was a rape claim.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.510
It was a rape case all along
and the jury rejected that,

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:37.950
but made other findings,

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.525
so we'll obviously be
appealing those other findings.

00:02:41.525 --> 00:02:42.358
(crowd cheers)

00:02:42.358 --> 00:02:44.040
- [Ramey] He's also sure to
face questions about the verdict

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.180
as he continues running

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.510
for the 2024 Republican
presidential nomination.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.060
It just compounds the various legal issues

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.820
that surround him right now.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:55.403
(bright music)

